  "scope": "# Frozen exit fallback after veto\nOnly a queried handback for which all three exits failed admission may change. Keep H75, R9, the five approach choices, initial planner, calibrated clearance margin, published exits, gate, physical clock and success definition. The incumbent arm reproduces the expanded-library C-R. The candidate uses the nearest five verified R9 handbacks from the same layout and approach route, using measured relock state only; choose the lowest physical contact count, then the highest complete-contract count for the assigned gate, then retain the incumbent for ties. No admission is issued by fallback. Prior skill outcomes for all three physically executed exits come from previously disclosed T3-transfer starts 1041\u20131070. Remove the complete target root in the development replay. Report all three maps, same-approach unavoidable contacts, completion rescues/losses and root-paired intervals. No result lookup by test root, force or future state at runtime.\nConfirm once on first 50 unused bank starts 1071\u20131120, same three known wall maps, three pushes and three left gates. Two live arms and 15 physical oracle exits, 3150 environments per map, 9450 total; no model training. Declare an engineering adoption criterion before looking at validation outcomes: fewer wall contacts overall (paired 95% upper bound below zero), completion difference lower 95% bound above minus 5 percentage points, unchanged admissions. Report per-layout regressions. Estimate query latency separately; retain the previously charged 15/15 ms for both arms. If insufficient, keep the incumbent and diagnose errors before freezing any further independent test.\n\nDevelopment iteration, before any new-root simulation. The first selector lost 49 completions while reducing contacts by 14. Refine it to switch only if the five neighbours predict strictly fewer collisions and at least as many completed contracts as keeping the existing fallback. Within eligible alternatives retain the original ranking. Eligibility uses same-root-excluded votes in the development replay; the independent comparison and thresholds above are unchanged.\n",
